item.text:
Wave 1 ledger: about 40 candidates screened, 18 documents opened, 10 source-claim units accepted, with several direct-fetch blockers on `government.ru` and some `rosstat.gov.ru` pages (timeouts / 502s). I used accessible Reuters, IMF, Interfax, RBC, CBR, ConsultantPlus, Euronews, and Freedom House pages to avoid repeating the same story.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin tips central bank chief Nabiullina for third term to ensure economic stability","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-18","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-putin-proposes-to-reappoint-central-bank-chief-nabiullina-2787264","claim":"Putin proposed nominating Elvira Nabiullina for a third term as Bank of Russia governor to ensure macroeconomic stability and preserve the central bank's inflation-fighting role.","locator":"L406-L413","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with direct attribution and clear policy context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; direct March 2022 personnel decision inside the ruler period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Putin proposal, although implementation still depended on parliamentary confirmation and central-bank action.","contrary_evidence":["Stability still depended heavily on emergency controls and sanctions-driven trade revenues."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders new budget rules to boost Russia's growth","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-orders-new-budget-rules-to-boost-russias-growth-2834324","claim":"Putin ordered the government to draw up new budget rules to boost growth and protect the economy from a serious downturn, saying the rules should stabilize public finances and raise growth rates.","locator":"L420-L424","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters report with a direct Putin quote and clear dated policy action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; direct June 2022 ruler action.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Putin instruction on fiscal rules and macro strategy.","contrary_evidence":["The rule change unfolded under sanctions pressure and a war-driven downturn, so it was partly reactive stabilization rather than clean long-run reform."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin throws lifeline to housing sector with subsidised mortgages extension","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-12-15","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-throws-lifeline-to-housing-sector-with-subsidised-mortgages-extension-2965444","claim":"Putin extended Russia's preferential mortgage scheme across the country until July 1, 2024, raising the subsidized rate to 8% from 7% and keeping 6% mortgages for families with at least two children.","locator":"L426-L430","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with direct Putin quote and concrete program terms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; direct December 2022 policy action.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Putin decision affecting household credit access and construction demand.","contrary_evidence":["The measure was a targeted subsidy to support a strained sector, not a structural fix to broader growth weaknesses."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.4","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders benefit payments for people arriving in Russia from Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-27","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/putin-orders-benefit-payments-for-people-arriving-in-russia-from-ukraine-2881261","claim":"Putin signed a decree introducing financial benefits for people forced to leave Ukrainian territory for Russia, including monthly pension payments of 10,000 roubles and one-off support for pregnant women and disabled people.","locator":"L419-L423","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report based on a government portal decree and direct presidential attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; direct August 2022 decree.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Putin order, though the policy is conflict-linked and targeted at displaced people from occupied or Russian-linked areas.","contrary_evidence":["The measure is narrow and conflict-tied, so it does not by itself show broad prosperity policy."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"On 2022 year a moratorium was introduced on some planned inspections of SMEs","publisher":"ConsultantPlus","publication_date":"2021-09-10","url":"https://www.consultant.ru/law/hotdocs/70917.html","claim":"A rule applicable in 2022 imposed a moratorium on some planned inspections of small and medium-sized businesses, with exceptions for high-risk activity and some licensing and audit cases.","locator":"L36-L44","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Legal summary of a formal government decree; the rule is explicit even though the page is a secondary legal digest.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Rule applied in 2022; source published in 2021 as a legal summary of the 2022 inspection moratorium.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution through the government regulatory regime under Putin, not a personal presidential act in this source.","contrary_evidence":["High-risk and some licensable activities remained subject to inspection, so the moratorium was partial rather than blanket deregulation."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's 2022 economic fall seen in lower incomes, slumping consumer demand","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2023-02-08","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-2022-economic-fall-seen-in-lower-incomes-slumping-consumer-demand-2998520","claim":"Reuters reported Rosstat data showing Russian consumer demand contracted at its fastest pace in seven years in 2022, real disposable incomes fell 1%, and retail sales fell 6.7%.","locator":"L406-L414","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters summary of official Rosstat data with clear quantitative claims.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospective 2023 report on full-year 2022 outcomes.","ruler_attribution":"Partly attributable to Putin-era policy and war shock, but strongly confounded by sanctions, mobilization, and external market conditions.","contrary_evidence":["Unemployment remained at a record low 3.7%, so the household picture was mixed rather than uniformly collapsing."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian consumer inflation slows to 12% as central bank meeting looms","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/next/2022/12/09/russia-cpi","claim":"Annual inflation in Russia slowed to 11.98% in November 2022, still far above the Bank of Russia's 4% target, and Reuters noted that households viewed inflation as a major living-standards concern.","locator":"L662-L666, L675-L691","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-sourced release of official Rosstat inflation data with a precise annual figure.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; November 2022 inflation snapshot inside the ruler period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution, because war, sanctions, and monetary tightening all contributed to the inflation path.","contrary_evidence":["The inflation rate was falling from earlier peaks, so the year showed stabilization as well as severe price pressure."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rosstat adjusts Russian poverty level for 2022 to 9.8% from 10.5%","publisher":"RBC","publication_date":"2023-05-03","url":"https://www.rbc.ru/economics/03/05/2023/6450f3239a79470733593138","claim":"RBC reported that Rosstat revised 2022 poverty to 9.8% and said the income ratio between the top 10% and bottom 10% fell to 13.8, attributing the improvement to targeted social support and higher transfers.","locator":"L213-L223","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Report cites Rosstat's revised 2022 figures and explicitly links the change to targeted support measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective 2023 report on 2022 household outcomes.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material attribution through Putin-era social spending and transfer policy; not a clean ruler-only causal proof.","contrary_evidence":["The improvement occurred amid war, sanctions, and a real-income squeeze, so it is not a clean prosperity boom."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"WEO Update July 2022 Press Briefing Transcript","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-07-27","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/07/27/tr072622-weo-uptate-july-22-press-briefing-transcript","claim":"The IMF said Russia's domestic economy had been doing fairly well because measures taken at the onset of the war, especially on the financial and monetary side, were effective, and strong oil and gas export revenues also helped support the outlook.","locator":"L355-L356","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF transcript quoting IMF staff directly and tying performance to early stabilization measures.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; July 2022 assessment of 2022 conditions.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution, since the IMF credits the policy response and export revenues rather than Putin personally, but it is relevant to the ruler-period record.","contrary_evidence":["The same IMF answer still described the outlook as a fairly severe recession, not a clean success story."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia: Nations in Transit 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022-06-01","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/russia/nations-transit/2022","claim":"Freedom House said Russia remained deeply corrupt and that access to public employees' personal assets and finances had been constrained by presidential decree, which the report said was meant to block independent investigations into grand corruption.","locator":"L291-L296","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Country report synthesizes the corruption environment and cites the decree-based disclosure restrictions directly.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022 country report covering the ruler period and its immediate baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Putin's control of disclosure rules and elite capture environment.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes an anti-corruption plan existed, so the picture is one of constrained, not absent, anti-corruption governance."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bank of Russia measures to support credit institutions","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-02-28","url":"https://cbr.ru/eng/press/pr/?file=28022022_075120FINSTAB_E28022022_174738.htm","claim":"The Bank of Russia loosened loan-provisioning and capital-buffer rules and recommended restructuring loans to cushion sanctions pressure and keep credit institutions able to lend to the economy.","locator":"L47-L53","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank press release with explicit dated policy actions and rationale.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; immediate post-invasion stabilization response.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional and indirect rather than personal-Putin attribution, but still part of the ruler-period economic response architecture.","contrary_evidence":["These were emergency defenses against sanctions shock, not evidence of preexisting structural strength."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9"]}
